From c89dbfeb97c2f6155de548fad9ce8554f7b6fd99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:03:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: the unit roster, 76 types in seven eras with one
 strength and class counters

Implements notes/freeciv45/design/units-and-upgrades.md section 1 (the roster)
on the civ45 ruleset:

- 16 new units (Scout, Axemen, Horse Bowmen, War Galley, Macebearers,
  Longbowmen, Crossbowmen, Trebuchet, Grenadiers, Ship of the Line, Infantry,
  Machine Gunners, Armoured Cars, Main Battle Tank, Air Defence Infantry, Jet
  Fighter), each with the graphic tag u.<name> and the template unit's graphic
  as graphic_alt until the tileset has sprites.
- 11 units renamed in the shown name only, keeping rule_name so saves, effects
  and scripts load: Phalanx (Spearmen), Legion (Swordsmen), Elephants (War
  Elephants), Armor (Tank), Nuclear (Atom Bomb), Mech. Inf. (Mechanized
  Infantry), Helicopter (Gunship), AWACS (Radar Plane), AEGIS Cruiser (Missile
  Cruiser), SSBN (Missile Submarine), ICBM (Nuclear Missile).
- Jaguar Warrior, Immortal, Alpine Troops, Crusaders and Mechanic removed;
  Engineers take over the Heal Unit enabler.
- One strength number for attack and defence (0 attack where the design says
  so), hit points 10 in eras I-III, 20 in IV-VI, 30 for armour, capital ships
  and era VII, firepower 1 everywhere; costs, moves, cargo, fuel and
  bombard_rate from the design tables; tech and resource requirements from
  the design, resources limited to the extras the map has (Iron, Coal, Ivory,
  Oil).
- Eight class flags (Melee, Archer, Mounted, Gun, Siege, Armour, Naval, Recon)
  and the counters as bonuses rows on the unit that has one, keyed on the
  target class: DefenseMultiplierPct when that class attacks it and
  DefenseDividerPct when it attacks that class (common/combat.c
  defense_multiplication reads the defender's rows against the attacker's
  flags and the attacker's rows against the defender's flags).
- effects.ruleset: Attack_Bonus against cities for twelve types, Armoured
  Cars' open-field bonus, Fortify_Defense_Bonus for Archers and Longbowmen in
  cities and Longbowmen and Partisans on rough ground, and City Walls keyed on
  the attacker's Melee, Archer, Mounted or Siege flag (not the Howitzer)
  instead of the Ground class.
- Caravel carries one Small Land unit and is no longer a barbarian boat (the
  server wants room for a leader and one man); Trireme keeps that role.
---
 data/civ45/README.civ45    |   38 +-
 data/civ45/actions.ruleset |    2 +-
 data/civ45/effects.ruleset |  205 +++++-
 data/civ45/units.ruleset   | 1227 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 4 files changed, 1093 insertions(+), 379 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/civ45/README.civ45 b/data/civ45/README.civ45
index d50a3a5..fd3a33c 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -30,8 +30,8 @@ Differences from sandbox
 - Cultural victory is enabled alongside spacerace and allied victory.
 - Combat is to the death: a fight lasts until the attacker or the
   defender dies (sandbox stops every fight after 15 rounds). Units with
-  the Withdraws flag (Horsemen, Chariot, Elephants, Crusaders, Knights,
-  Dragoons, Cavalry, Armor) break off their own attacks instead, after
+  the Withdraws flag (Horsemen, Chariot, Horse Bowmen, Knights, Dragoons,
+  Cavalry, Armoured Cars) break off their own attacks instead, after
   12 rounds for every 10 hit points they have left; when attacked they
   fight to the death like everyone else.
 - Siege collateral: Catapult, Cannon, Artillery and Howitzer (flag
@@ -71,11 +71,35 @@ Differences from sandbox
   the whip too: disbanded in a city ("Disband recovering production")
   each puts 30 shields into the build, whatever it cost, so a citizen
   becomes 30 shields. No unhappiness follows a draft yet.
-- Strategic resources: Legion needs Iron and Armor needs Oil somewhere in
-  the city's radius.
-- Nation-unique units and buildings: Aztec Jaguar Warrior (replaces
-  Warriors, attack 2, ignores terrain), Persian Immortal (replaces Legion,
-  defence 3, no Iron needed), Arab Bazaar (built on a Marketplace, +50%
+- The roster: 76 unit types over seven eras (notes/freeciv45/design/
+  units-and-upgrades.md), with one strength number for attack and
+  defence (0 attack for scouts, transports, machine gunners, air
+  defence and the radar plane), 10 hit points in the first three eras,
+  20 in the next three and 30 for armour, capital ships and the last
+  era, firepower 1 throughout. Class flags (Melee, Archer, Mounted, Gun,
+  Siege, Armour, Naval, Recon) key the counters, two bonuses rows on
+  the unit that has one (DefenseMultiplierPct when that class attacks
+  it, DefenseDividerPct when it attacks that class): Spearmen and
+  Pikemen are twice as strong against mounted units, Axemen,
+  Macebearers and Crossbowmen half again against hand-weapon foot,
+  mounted units half again against siege engines, Mechanized Infantry
+  half again and the Gunship twice against armour, and so on; siege
+  units, Swordsmen, Marines, tanks and big ships get an
+  attack bonus against cities; Archers and Longbowmen hold cities,
+  Longbowmen and Partisans hills. City Walls double the defence only
+  against Melee, Archer, Mounted and Siege attackers (not the Howitzer).
+  Renamed units keep their old rule_name (Phalanx is Spearmen, Legion
+  Swordsmen, Elephants War Elephants, Armor Tank, Nuclear Atom Bomb,
+  Mech. Inf. Mechanized Infantry, Helicopter Gunship, AWACS Radar Plane,
+  AEGIS Cruiser Missile Cruiser, SSBN Missile Submarine, ICBM Nuclear
+  Missile), so saves and scripts load. Jaguar Warrior, Immortal, Alpine
+  Troops, Crusaders and Mechanic are gone (Engineers heal vehicles).
+- Strategic resources: Swordsmen, Macebearers, Crossbowmen, Knights,
+  Cannon, Ship of the Line and Ironclad need Iron (Ironclad Coal too),
+  War Elephants Ivory, and armour, aircraft and modern warships Oil,
+  somewhere in the city's radius. Horses, copper, aluminium and uranium
+  wait for the resources slice.
+- Nation-unique buildings: Arab Bazaar (built on a Marketplace, +50%
   luxury, +25% gold). No new graphics yet; they reuse the sprites of the
   unit or building they replace.
 
